id: pm-vcs-6ihf
title: Retain explicit topological ordering for rewrite ranges
description: Decide whether topoSort is redundant or a required safety property after coverage showed its parent-queue arm had not previously executed.
type: Decision
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: architecture,coverage,history-rewrite,ordering
created_at: "2026-07-31T11:43:39.209Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T11:44:02.046Z"
deadline: "2026-08-01T11:43:39.209Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-31T11:44:02.023Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-31T11:44:02.023Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 15
acceptance_criteria: "Decision names the ordering invariant, alternatives, evidence, and consequence; a multi-commit rebase test fails if newest-first discovery order is replayed directly; full coverage reaches 100/100/100"
resolution: Retain the iterative parent-before-child traversal with push-time deduplication.
expected_result: Rewrite ranges replay every parent before its children without recursion or reliance on Set discovery order.
actual_result: "The multi-commit rebase test executes the parent queue, preserves both change identities, and the 341-test gate reaches 100/100/100."
