comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T11:43:39.209Z","harness:codex",The new two-commit rebase test executes topoSort's parent queue and asserts the older change is replayed onto the new base before its child.
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T11:43:39.209Z","harness:codex","The traversal is a correctness boundary, not coverage scaffolding: deleting it would apply a child before its rewritten parent exists."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T11:43:39.209Z","harness:codex","Reachability order and replay order have opposite semantics: graph discovery starts at the tip, while replay must start at the oldest included ancestor."
files[1]{path,scope,note}:
